From 189630321ce4b480cc8f2e304ae226563017785e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:27:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diglett's Cave Dugtrio under the level cap, Nuzlocke poison
 check (R24)

- Diglett's Cave Dugtrio are Lv. 27-28 (were 29 and 31), so nothing
  catchable before Lt. Surge is above his level cap (28).
- Playtest: nuzlocke_poison - a field-poison black-out after a Trainer
  Tower loss ends the run (fails without release 23's fix). 26 checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JQmLEZftLdDmGYX3wiQ71G
---
 HACK_NOTES.md                   |  8 +++++---
 include/hack_version.h          |  2 +-
 src/data/wild_encounters.json   | 16 ++++++++--------
 tools/hack/playtest/playtest.py | 13 +++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/HACK_NOTES.md b/HACK_NOTES.md
index cf9b1fb..b94bf30 100644
--- a/HACK_NOTES.md
+++ b/HACK_NOTES.md
@@ -434,6 +434,8 @@ How the cap works with each way of gaining levels:
   Pokémon Tower, the Safari Zone, Power Plant, Seafoam Islands, Pokémon
   Mansion, the Sevii Islands 1–3, Route 23, Victory Road (now up to Lv. 55)
   and Cerulean Cave. Fishing levels are unchanged.
+- Diglett's Cave's Dugtrio are Lv. 27–28 (they were Lv. 29 and 31), so
+  nothing you can catch before Lt. Surge is above his level cap.
 - **VS Seeker rematches catch up:**
   - **When:** until you have all eight badges.
   - **What:** any route rematch Pokémon below 5 levels under the next Gym
@@ -595,7 +597,7 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
   Tower team is fully evolved with no repeated species or item, and no
   Lv. 50+ trainer Pokémon is left unevolved (level-up or classic
   stone/item/trade/friendship evolutions; any evolution at Lv. 75+).
-- `playtest/playtest.py [check ...]`: automated playtest. It runs 25 milestone
+- `playtest/playtest.py [check ...]`: automated playtest. It runs 26 milestone
   checks in a headless mGBA:
   - The boot menu.
   - A wild battle stopping at the level cap.
@@ -612,8 +614,8 @@ Each script runs once against the original pret data:
     Master Ball limit and the PP Up trade too).
   - The peak Champion's battle.
   - The Gym Leader rematch and Elite Four round 3 rewards.
-  - Nuzlocke blackouts: an ordinary loss ends the run, and a peak trainer
-    loss doesn't.
+  - Nuzlocke blackouts: an ordinary loss ends the run, a peak trainer loss
+    doesn't, and a field-poison black-out after a Trainer Tower loss does.
   - Party Exp. Share.
 
   Each check reads the game's memory to confirm it worked. Build the harness first with
